### Final acceptance record

The final configured test review found a test-only failure-path ownership gap: temporarily removing the inventory composer could prevent fixture disposal if an assertion failed. The configured test writer restored that composer in `finally` around the complete zero-surface act/assert section. Independent re-review confirmed success/failure-path ownership without weakening assertions or introducing double disposal. The remaining final test-review conclusions were clean.

Final delegated verification used SDK 10.0.401, net10.0, VSTest, and xUnit v2 with the existing game references:

```powershell
dotnet test .\VanillaExpanded.Tests\VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj --framework net10.0 --verbosity minimal --filter "FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookLayoutLifecycleTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookLayoutCacheTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookLayoutTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookTileGeometryTests|FullyQualifiedName~GuiLayoutInputsTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookDialogLayoutTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookLayoutCacheDialogTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookOptionsTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookBrowsingRestorationTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookDialogCleanupTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookOpenerStateTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookSystemLifecycleTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookDialogFeedbackTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookSearchClearTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookTilesGeometryTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookTilesInteractionTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookNativeBoundsCompatibilityTests|FullyQualifiedName~NativeTranslationCacheCompatibilityTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookDialogNativeInputTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookTileNativeInputTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookNativePopupLayeringTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookNativeTooltipIntegrationTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookInventoryRefreshIntegrationTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookSessionOwnershipTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookSessionProjectionTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookCategoryPresentationTests"
```

Both the initial final batch and the rerun after the ownership correction passed **380 tests, 0 failed, 0 skipped**. The mod DLL built successfully. The latest run surfaced 29 existing warnings: CS8602 (23), CS8603 (4), CS8604 (1), and xUnit2031 (1). The earlier run surfaced 36 warnings; these are not warning-free build claims or claims that this phase fixed unrelated warnings. No packages, manifests, release generation, or game-reference changes were needed.

