Runtime acceptance limitation: this session has no interactive native-game window driver or controlled live test world. No game was launched or world opened for acceptance. The two concrete in-game check groups above remain **blocked/unverified**; the parent smoke-check requirement uses its explicit availability-blocker alternative. Live visual/GPU behavior and measured frame-time improvements remain unverified. No functional proposal requirement is deferred; the limitation is the unavailable live acceptance surface.

[RecipeBook.md](RecipeBook.md#cached-shell-layout) now describes the current architecture, dependencies, language contract, conditional composition, root translation, and state/resource boundaries with a flow diagram and pseudocode. README remains player-focused and unchanged. The second documentation review checked these claims against the implementation. Mermaid syntax was reviewed against its flowchart documentation; the validator tool timed out, so an automated rendered-preview check is unavailable.

Cleanup inventory: no temporary working-note, interim-analysis, or handoff documents were created; the session artifact directory was empty and the initial worktree had no untracked files. Retain this plan, the architecture guide, and regression support. Scoped test counters/counting bounds/native compatibility fixtures are necessary ongoing verification support, not disposable diagnostics; no production per-frame diagnostic instrumentation or engine patches were introduced. The only final-phase source change is the test ownership correction; other final-phase changes are this retained record and architecture documentation.

Independent completion audit: the fresh read-only reviewer applied the stage-completion audit directly to the plan, inherited sources, implementation, tests, and documentation and concluded that Phase 4 is fully satisfied with no required gaps. The reviewer confirmed the direct 1,000-frame assertions, corrected test ownership, documentation accuracy, and the explicit smoke-blocker alternative. The two live-check children remain unchecked and labeled blocked/unverified; no live/GPU/frame-time acceptance is implied. Local documentation validation passed for 74 targets, and whitespace checks passed. Completion markers were updated only after this verdict.
